From f59d83501a32f17336b9edb313a2c06ac4cb2752 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caeliglow-validate <caeliglow@local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:42:37 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] caeliglow: install updates in place with a live progress bar,
 no terminal

The About page's "Install" action now downloads, rebuilds and applies a new
CaeliGlow release without opening a terminal, streaming live progress into the
card and restarting the running shell into the new version when it finishes.

- installUpdate() launches the same quick-install one-liner that first installed
  CaeliGlow, but fully detached (double-fork + setsid) so it survives the shell's
  own restart, redirecting all output to ~/.cache/caeliglow/update.log.
- The About card polls that log on a 250 ms main-loop Timer and drives a native
  ProgressBar plus a phase Label directly, so no worker-thread marshaling is
  needed. On the exit sentinel it reports success or the captured error.
- caeliglow/update_model.hpp gains a pure, side-effect-free parseInstallProgress()
  that turns captured installer output into a 0..1 fraction and a phase label
  (download 0.05-0.35, build 0.36-0.85, install 0.87, restart 0.95), watching the
  CAELIGLOW_UPDATE_EXIT sentinel for completion.
- tests/update_model_test.cpp covers both the update decision logic and the new
  progress parser (registered in meson.build; suite is 155/155).
- Privilege elevation moves to a TTY-aware escalator in the installer: sudo when
  run from a terminal, otherwise a graphical polkit prompt via pkexec.
